# Never commit somebody's photographs. This repository is public and git
# history is permanent. A phone photo carries GPS coordinates, a timestamp and
# a face, and the EXIF parser in this package exists precisely because that
# data is there.
#
# There are no binary fixtures at all, which is why there is no rule for them
# here. Every test buffer is built in code from the format's specification, so
# the suite runs on a clean checkout and a wrong expectation shows up in the
# diff rather than hiding inside a file nobody can read.
#
# Real files used for measurement, and anything generated to check this
# package against ImageMagick or ffmpeg, belong in scratch/, which is ignored.
scratch/
*.private.*
real-*.heic
real-*.HEIC
real-*.png
real-*.jpg
real-*.jpeg
